    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d172">

                <pb facs="0198" n="186" sameAs="frus:frus1946v08/pg186"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00115 PW/3–2946</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Officer in Charge of the Office of the Political
                        Adviser in Japan to the Department of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 340</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-03-29">March 29, 1946</date>.<lb/>[Received April
                        8.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Officer in Charge has the honor to forward copies, in quadruplicate, of a
                    memorandum from the Supreme Commander for the Allied Powers to the Japanese
                    Government, dated March 16, 1946,<anchor n="48" xml:id="d172-f1"/> which sets
                    forth basic instructions covering the repatriation of Japanese nationals from
                    the areas of the various military commanders in the Far East and of displaced
                    persons in Japan formerly domiciled in China, Formosa, and the Ryukyus. This
                    directive supersedes all previous instructions to the Japanese Government on the
                    general subject of repatriation.</p>
                <p>It will be noted that the directive will not apply to the repatriation of
                    Japanese nationals from the areas under the military control of the Commander in
                    Chief of Soviet Forces in the Far East until appropriate agreements have been
                    consummated.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
